{"term":"charming","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:68df1d03576f4d6748","definition":"Pleasant, charismatic.","example":"\"What a charming amusement for young people this is, Mr. Darcy! There is nothing like dancing after all. I consider it as one of the first refinements of polished society.\"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["charismatic","smart","witty","taking","fetching","captivating"],"antonyms":["dull","charmless"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["charmingly","charmingness","Prince Charming","ultracharming","uncharming"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charming#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:32017b7f506501e351","definition":"Delightful in a playful way which avoids responsibility or seriousness, as if attracting through a magical charm.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["silly","charmless"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["charmingly","charmingness","Prince Charming","ultracharming","uncharming"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charming#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8035531777512c21d2","definition":"present participle and gerund of charm","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"form-of, gerund, participle, present","register":"form-of, gerund, participle, present","wordFamily":["charmingly","charmingness","Prince Charming","ultracharming","uncharming"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charming#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:52cdf77c5650a95445","definition":"The casting of a magical charm.","example":"They denied me often flour, barm and milk, / Goose-grease and tar, when I ne'er hurt their charmings, / Thei